      "problem": "Find the differential $\\text{d}f$ for the function $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3}).$",
      "worked_solution": "We compute the differential using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y,z) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{∂f}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\,\\text{d}x}{{x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3}}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{{x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3}}+\\frac{3{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}z}{{x}^{2}+y+{z}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
